1	//! Prime Winding — the winding_period_of_the_primes_on_the_number_line ob3ect
2	//! as a kernel command.
3	//!
4	//! The ob3ect's glyph word ⊢⊙∈≻⊤⋈≺⊥⊞∋⊡⋈⊙⊣ has period 14 and is phase-bearing
5	//! across A / Ftf / tf / T. The word, glyph, tuple, and cycle commands report
6	//! the Grammar's reading of a number. The primality verdict and factoring run
7	//! on real arithmetic: trial division then Miller-Rabin, deterministic below
8	//! 3,317,044,064,679,887,385,961,981 and the standard thirteen-witness practice
9	//! above it. In the GPU build the verdict runs on the device (see gpu_prime).
10	//! A Grammar-native verdict via the winding period and the ⊡ holonomy is the
11	//! open route, closing.
12	//!
13	//! Subcommands:
14	//!   prime_winding word                       canonical glyph word
15	//!   prime_winding find <n>                   nearest prime <= n
16	//!   prime_winding range <lo> <hi> [count]    every prime in [lo, hi]
17	//!   prime_winding factor <n>                 factor n into primes
18	//!   prime_winding cycle                      full ROTAT orbit, landing per cut
19	//!   prime_winding tuple                      the 12-slot tuple
20	//!   prime_winding verdict                    Frobenius verdict
21	//!   prime_winding help                       list subcommands
