29	/// Each hex nibble's canonical IMASM word, one word per bit pattern of
30	/// {T-bit, F-bit, I-bit, fork-openness-bit}, built from the ob3ect
31	/// "A hex digit's fourth bit as fork openness, not a fifth glyph"
32	/// (`ob3ect/digital/a_hex_digit_s_fourth_bit_as_fork_openness_not_a_f03510ea`).
33	/// v=0xF reproduces that ob3ect's own canonical word exactly — checked, not
34	/// assumed. The template: ⊢, then ∈ iff the fork bit is set, then ⊤ iff the
35	/// T-bit is set, then ≻⋈, then ⊥ iff the F-bit is set, then ≺ (the clear —
36	/// banked if the fork opened before it, exposed otherwise), then ⋈ and ∋
37	/// iff the fork bit is set, then ⊞ iff the I-bit is set, then ⊙⊡⊣.
38	/// Verified pairwise distinct across all 16 against the real kernel.
39	pub const HEX_WORDS: [&str; 16] = [
40	    "⊢≻⋈≺⊙⊡⊣",             // 0x0  T=0 F=0 I=0 fork=0
41	    "⊢⊤≻⋈≺⊙⊡⊣",           // 0x1  T=1 F=0 I=0 fork=0
42	    "⊢≻⋈⊥≺⊙⊡⊣",           // 0x2  T=0 F=1 I=0 fork=0
43	    "⊢⊤≻⋈⊥≺⊙⊡⊣",         // 0x3  T=1 F=1 I=0 fork=0
44	    "⊢≻⋈≺⊞⊙⊡⊣",           // 0x4  T=0 F=0 I=1 fork=0
45	    "⊢⊤≻⋈≺⊞⊙⊡⊣",         // 0x5  T=1 F=0 I=1 fork=0
46	    "⊢≻⋈⊥≺⊞⊙⊡⊣",         // 0x6  T=0 F=1 I=1 fork=0
47	    "⊢⊤≻⋈⊥≺⊞⊙⊡⊣",       // 0x7  T=1 F=1 I=1 fork=0
48	    "⊢∈≻⋈≺⋈∋⊙⊡⊣",         // 0x8  T=0 F=0 I=0 fork=1
49	    "⊢∈⊤≻⋈≺⋈∋⊙⊡⊣",       // 0x9  T=1 F=0 I=0 fork=1
50	    "⊢∈≻⋈⊥≺⋈∋⊙⊡⊣",       // 0xA  T=0 F=1 I=0 fork=1
51	    "⊢∈⊤≻⋈⊥≺⋈∋⊙⊡⊣",     // 0xB  T=1 F=1 I=0 fork=1
52	    "⊢∈≻⋈≺⋈⊞∋⊙⊡⊣",       // 0xC  T=0 F=0 I=1 fork=1
53	    "⊢∈⊤≻⋈≺⋈⊞∋⊙⊡⊣",     // 0xD  T=1 F=0 I=1 fork=1
54	    "⊢∈≻⋈⊥≺⋈⊞∋⊙⊡⊣",     // 0xE  T=0 F=1 I=1 fork=1
55	    "⊢∈⊤≻⋈⊥≺⋈⊞∋⊙⊡⊣",   // 0xF  T=1 F=1 I=1 fork=1 -- the ob3ect's own word
56	];
